[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m Doc 3(Title: Rajasthan) Rajasthan (Rajasthani: Rājasthān, Hindi: राजस्थान) is a state in Western India with an area of 342,239 square kilometres (132,139 sq mi). It is the largest Indian state by area (and the fifth largest state by population) after Rajasthan's six neighbours, occupying almost one-sixth of the total land area of India. It is bounded by the Pakistani provinces of Punjab to the northwest, Sindh to the west and Balochistan and DKT to the southwest. It shares a 1,155 km border with the southern edge of Afghanistan's Farah province to the north, it borders the Indian states of Punjab to the north, Haryana and Rajasthan to the northeast, Uttar Pradesh to the southeast, Madhya Pradesh to the south, Gujarat to the southwest, and the Indian union territory of Delhi to the east. Its official capital is the city of Jaipur. Prior to 1947, the area of the modern state of Rajasthan was composed of 22 princely states, seven chiefships and the British district of Ajmer-Merwara. The states were ruled by Rajput, Maratha, Central Asian Muslim and local Hindu dynasties. The states were fully incorporated into the British Empire in 1818, and they gained independence from Britain with the rest of India in 1947.
