[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m Doc 4(Title: Scooby-Doo characters) Scooby-Doo characters The main characters of ""Scooby-Doo"" are four teenage teenagers and their Great Dane dog: Fred Jones, Daphne Blake, Velma Dinkley, Shaggy Rogers, and Scooby-Doo. Fred Jones is the team leader, responsible for both orchestrating each scheme and disguising himself as whatever will be the alleged killer for the episode. He also uses his persona as a television personality to explain clues, and the solution to the mystery, at the end of the episode. Scooby-Doo is Fred's best friend, and a Great Dane whose intelligence is sometimes displayed despite his name. He has a human-like body and a unique tail that he can use as a hangman's noose. Shaggy Rogers (thought of as ""Shaggy"" for short) is a wise crack comedian, and often needs the help of Scooby-Doo, after eating what he thinks is the monster, only to discover that it's really a funny-looking, benign human. Daphne Blake is an ambitious and tomboyish reporter. Velma Dinkley is a very intelligent girl with a huge passion for science, puzzles, and mysteries. Fred's unique way of confronting the "bad guys" always leaves them surprised, and he is responsible for the team to get away using a trap or disguise.
