[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m Doc 4(Title: "The Simpsons") "The Simpsons" is an American animated sitcom created by Matt Groening for the Fox Broadcasting Company. The series is a satirical depiction of working-class life epitomized by the Simpson family, which consists of Homer, Marge, Bart, Lisa, and Maggie. The show is set in the fictional town of Springfield and parodies American culture, society, television, and the human condition. Matt Groening conceived the idea for the series while working on "Life in Hell" during the 1980s. Groening developed The Simpsons in collaboration with James L. Brooks and Sam Simon, who served as co-executive producers for the first five seasons. With the full support of 20th Century Fox and James L. Brooks, Groening used his position to implement a management style that empowered the show's writers, leading to the creation of many references and gags that defined the show. As the series progressed, it moved away from its satirical roots and focused on more character-driven storytelling. The series also started to incorporate episodes based on popular films and television shows.
