[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m Doc 2(Title: Childhood and education) Juggernaut was born in Panipat into a Brahmin family on 8 June 1959. It was his fifth and last child of his parents, H.B. and Suchitra Joshi. He grew up alongside his elder siblings, Laxmikant, Shriram, Deepak, Prabhakant, and Mahesh, who all grew to become television personalities, artists, directors and writers. In 1972, Juggernaut played his first leading role on the screen, in the film Jai Maa Annapurna, a comedy-set in the 18th century.
[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m As a child, Juggernaut was also trained as an actor by his father, who later composed the songs for the series Omkar Kaan, starring his brother Mahesh Joshi. His father also co-founded Vidaarshni Theater, which educated children. With the help of his parents, brother Laxmikant, and friends Shivshankar and Dinesh Bhatt, Juggernaut established the Chakravyuh drama school and theatre organization in 1980. The drama school was based in Delhi. Here, Juggernaut was mentored by Santosh Joshi (H B's brother-in-law). The theatre went on to produce several plays and playscripts, which often focused on political, historical, and contemporary events. During this time, he acted in 20 plays, directed 20 plays, and wrote over 10 playscripts.
[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m 
