[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m The Woolworths Group, commonly known as Woolies, was the largest retailer in Australia and a major chain in New Zealand. However, it no longer exists in its original form due to liquidation. The company filed for administration on December 17, 2019, and it was announced that the brand was to be liquidated. The liquidation process was completed in June 2020.
[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m Previously, in the UK, Woolworths was acquired by Home Retail Group (HRG), which operated the Homebase and B&Q brands, in April 2008. In October 2009, the UK subsidiary of Woolworths was sold to Firmdale Holdings, a South African company. Following a receivership process, the UK operation was sold to a consortium of investors led by Canadian retail giant H.2O Group in June 2012. This led to a rebranding, and the UK business was renamed High End Retail Group. However, financial difficulties forced the company to enter administration in April 2017. The business was subsequently sold to a Canadian pension fund.
