[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m Doc 1(Title: "History of Surfwear") The iconic 1962 creation of Hawaiian designer Izzy Darney may have just the right amount of '60s- and '70s-style attitude to wear when watching the documentary on his life and times. When Darney was a junior in high school in the late 1950s, he saw a Hawaiian shirt worn by a student on the campus. Imprinted on the shirt was the phrase "Live Well, Love Deep, Get Real," and Darney loved it. He sold Honolulu surfer Warren "Moondog" Gilmore on his idea and they started making shirts together. The first garment they made, however, was a beach kimono that Gilmore had designed.
