[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m Doc 2(Title: "History of Surfwear") The notion that some clothing items are timeless has yet to gain traction with marketers. Their money is invested in seasonal advertising campaigns. Has there ever been a time in retail history when consumers didn't seek the clothes, shoes, and accessories of the moment, at least at higher price points? Has there ever been an era in which the ordinary sweater, cardigan, and t-shirt didn't quickly become the most popular pieces in the wardrobes of most men and women? Certainly not. Perhaps the closest we've come to witnessing a true transition from clothing types based on seasons to clothing types based on fashion were the years between the 1890s and 1920s.
