[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m Doc 4(Title: "History - Titanic - How did the Titanic Sink") How Did the Titanic Sink? "The film makes mention of the ships final moments, so we thought we'd take the opportunity to explain just how the Titanic sank. The story starts out like most of the greatest adventures; with love, a marriage, a grand honeymoon, and an idea to build the worlds greatest ship, the Titanic." "The Titanic hit the iceberg and took on water through the hull plates. Water entered the front compartment and filled it in about 35 minutes. Since the Titanic was not ready for launching the two lifeboats to port at this time, the forward compartment filled to its full capacity and the ship started to list to port, filling the adjoining compartment." "As the Titanic started to sink water rushed forward from the compartments and into the adjacent compartments. When the weight of the water eventually became more than the buoyancy of the ship then it would sink, about 150 minutes after impact." The Titanic struck an iceberg at 11:40 pm on 14th April 1912. This is what she looks like below the water line as she struck the iceberg. Here you can see the forward point of the starboard side and the gash and holes that the iceberg made.
