[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m Vocalizations are produced by a vibrating vocal fold, either at the front of the larynx as is the case for "speaking" or at the back of the larynx for "singing". The vocal cords are made of two bands of mucous membranes supported by a framework of ligaments. Movements of the various muscles attached to the vocal cords change the shape of the cords and thereby change the pitch, or frequency of vibration, which determines the fundamental frequency of the sound.
[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m 
