[36m(main_task pid=2827894)[0m The US strategy during the Cold War was containment, which aimed to prevent the spread of communism and protect strategically vital regions. This involved supporting anti-communist governments and alliances like NATO, as well as engaging in proxy wars. Some key events during this time include the Korean War, the Vietnam War, and the Cuban Missile Crisis. The Cold War also had significant social and political impacts within the US, leading to the emergence of McCarthyism and concerns about Communist influence.
